                                            "A trinary star."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a3585b0-625f-35e2-bd3a-679fb351b9ef",
                                        "entry_id": "b0ac73f3-6997-316d-b0b1-6af191812ea2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ternary, a set of three things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "419e353e-548e-45d3-9b25-9df48fe3c7bc",
                                                "sense_id": "2a3585b0-625f-35e2-bd3a-679fb351b9ef",
                                                "text": "[…] a trinary of terms to describe conceived, perceived, and lived space."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec04ba9d-da28-4055-b450-3a10271c135f",
                                                "sense_id": "2a3585b0-625f-35e2-bd3a-679fb351b9ef",
                                                "text": "Collectively, religion, the secular, the superstition form what Josephson has called a \"trinary\" of mutually constitutive forces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7b15b1f-e9a5-431c-99e3-656b6b7aaa79",
                                                "sense_id": "2a3585b0-625f-35e2-bd3a-679fb351b9ef",
                                                "text": "[…] a trinary of expert, governed, and lived religion in order to study how the category of religion has come to be used in academic studies of global religion and secularity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
